    <item>
      <title>Achieving transformative recovery following natural disasters</title>
      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s43017-026-00863-2</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Reviews Earth &amp;amp; Environment, Published online: 20 November 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s43017-026-00863-2"&gt;doi:10.1038/s43017-026-00863-2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Natural disasters create pressure to rebuild quickly, but rushing to reinstate the status quo can restore or amplify the very exposures and inequities that contributed to losses. Recovery systems must aim to reduce future risk, centre equity, and integrate physical, social, economic, and environmental resilience across decades rather than funding cycles.</content:encoded>
